    "q-45188": {
      "dom_id": "step-q45188",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "The point $P(5,6)$ is rotated ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise about the origin $O$ and then translated according to the function $(x,y)↦(x+k,y+k).$ If the image of $P$ under this sequence of transformations is $(12,1),$ then $k=$",
      "worked_solution": "Let's apply the given transformations.\n\nA rotation of ${90}^{∘}$ clockwise about $O$ can be represented by\n\n$$\n(x,y)↦(y,-x).\n$$\n\nApplying this to the point $P,$ we get\n\n$$\n(5,6)↦(6,-5).\n$$\n\n \n\nNow, applying the translation to $(6,-5),$ we get\n\n$$\n(6,-5)↦(6+k,\\,-5+k).\n$$\n\n \n\nSince the resulting point is $(12,1),$ by equating the $x$- and $y$-coordinates, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\{\\begin{aligned}6+k=12 \\\\ -5+k=1\\end{aligned}\\,⟹\\,k & =6.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $k=6.$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
